course: dictionary
lesson: 12901
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words can do more than one job. «The workers erected a tall fence around the park.» Here erect is a verb, a doing word. To erect something means to build it or put it up, so the workers built the fence.
explain: «The meerkat stood erect, watching for danger.» Now erect is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you the meerkat was standing straight up. The sentence gives the clue: the meerkat was watching, so it was up on its feet.
explain: Look at the words around erect to find its job. If a word like «a fence», «a tent» or «a statue» comes after it, erect is probably a doing word. If it describes how something stands, like «stood erect» or «ears erect», it is probably a describing word.
fact: Erect is a verb when you build or put something up: erect, erects, erected, erecting.
fact: Erect is an adjective when it means standing straight up, or upright.
fact: Useful phrases include «erect a tent», «erect a monument» and «stand erect».
fact: «Erected» is the past tense: «The statue was erected in the square.»
fact: Formal texts, like signs and history books, often use erect for building things.
exercise: «The workers erected a tall fence around the park.» What does erected mean here? | Knocked down | Painted green | Sold cheaply | *Built or put up
exercise: «The meerkat stood erect, watching for danger.» What does erect mean here? | Lying flat on the ground | *Standing straight up | Hidden under a rock | Running very fast
exercise: «The dog's ears were erect when it heard a noise.» Find and copy one word that means standing up straight. | noise | heard | *erect | ears
test: «A statue was erected in the square to honour the hero.» What does erected mean? | Hid | *Built and put up | Drew a picture of | Took away
test: Ben asks, «What does stand erect mean?» | Fall over | Lie down flat | Jump high | *Stand up straight
exam: «They erected a tent before the rain started.» Which meaning fits erected? | Ate it | *Put it up | Took it down | Lost it
